+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+OFF retains common TF and legacy button following. ON shares Porter GAP1–4 with the planner and button decisions. With dedicated GAP ON, own speed sets the base distance and lead speed plus distance error continuously cap the button target. Reduce approach speed outside the gap; cap at or below lead speed inside it. Confirmed gap recovery permits bounded target restoration. Lower urgent targets are not delayed; brief lead dropouts or invalid inputs inhibit recovery. Confirmed absence of a lead permits bounded recovery after the 0.6s hold. Sub-30km/h cancellation and transmission limits remain.
+On Porter conventional cruise, a valid stock OFF followed by ON clears the preceding session’s GAP deceleration/recovery state and reevaluates current lead, planner and navigation limits. A CAN gap during continuous stock ON or an invalid OFF sample does not clear protection. Saved GAP values and transmission/cancel limits remain.
+Outside-gap approach prediction reserves the request time to lower the stock setting toward lead speed in 1km/h steps. Existing reductions inside the gap remain unchanged.
+
+After 0.5s gap confirmation, normal recovery is at most 1.8km/h per second. With sufficient gap and 1s of confirmed absence or opening faster than 0.2m/s, recovery toward the current comma target is bounded by request spacing and at most 3km/h per second. Lower lead, planner and navigation limits and transmission bounds remain; no direct braking is added.
+
+Range reserve alone cannot allow target recovery or RES+ while closing. A fresh plan requesting positive acceleration with no falling segment in its speed forecast and no stop, red-light or stop-preparation state may recover after 0.5s of confirmed projected gap, within existing rise limits. Brief relative-speed sign changes alone then cannot retain an old low target indefinitely. Lead dropouts, invalid inputs and insufficient gap still inhibit recovery; lower lead, planner and navigation targets pass immediately.
+Button targets, OEM settings and the lead allowance for pedal-release SET use dashboard km/h. Distance and relative motion use physical units before conversion by the speedometer ratio. An invalid ratio blocks target recovery and that SET; existing lead, navigation, cancellation and transmission limits remain.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Enable in Porter Only, then adjust the dedicated gaps and lookahead. Allow about five seconds for planner refresh; neither set of saved values is copied or reset.
+Short-tap the GAP number or green bars on the comma 3 driving screen to select 4→3→2→1→4. Holds and drags are ignored; edit time values in Web.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+GAP selection buttons and model-stop/navigation targets remain. Settings do not guarantee physical spacing, braking or stopping.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
