+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+During active system/cruise operation, selects dashboard speed at release rather than pedal peak. Other vehicles require about 0.4s on the pedal and a release speed above the previous comma setting.
+
+Porter conventional cruise uses a fresh press of at least 0.1s and release at least 1km/h above the OEM setting, taking priority over the short-tap preset. For example, comma 60/OEM 47 and release at 58 selects 58. Profiles 1025/15489 with SpeedFromPCM=0 request one SET− press (at most 3 frames/60ms) and release at the next fresh CAN opportunity only when planner, lead and navigation allow it; only stale GAP recovery memory is rebased.
+Button targets, OEM settings and the lead allowance for pedal-release SET use dashboard km/h. Distance and relative motion use physical units before conversion by the speedometer ratio. An invalid ratio blocks target recovery and that SET; existing lead, navigation, cancellation and transmission limits remain.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Use during existing cruise operation. Initial dispatch must start within 0.1s of release, with up to 0.5s for confirmation. The cue is not retried; another attempt requires 3s after the last transmission and a new pedal press. Brake, CANCEL, buttons, speed commands or loss of eligibility discard remaining input.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Current lead, model, curve and navigation limits and vehicle-owned PCM modes remain. The captured ceiling limits automatic road-speed increases and survives GAP changes; explicit speed input, cruise interruption or OFF clears it. Independent of the standby auto-SET toggle; actual ECU acceptance and speed-holding timing are not guaranteed.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
